--------------------The code provided is using Pex, a framework from Microsoft for automatic property-based testing. The "PUT_IndexOfContract" method is a property-based test for the "IndexOf" method of an ArrayList. The test checks whether the returned index is non-negative when the specified item is in the list, and the list counts of the old and new lists are equal. 

Here are the Assert statements based on the comments:

```cs
Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0); // The return value is non-negative
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount); // The new and old array counts are equal
```

The first assertion checks that the returned index is non-negative. If the IndexOf method returned a negative value, it means that the specified item was not found in the list. The second assertion makes sure that the count of the list remains the same before and after the "IndexOf" operation. The "Count" property of the ArrayList class returns the number of elements actually contained in the ArrayList.
